From: fedora-atomic-phone <noreply@fedora-atomic-phone.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-dai: accept S32_LE playback

The OnePlus 12 speaker back end (SECONDARY_MI2S_RX, two TFA9874 amps)
runs 2 x 32-bit I2S slots (patch 0003). q6apm-dai offers only S16_LE and
S24_LE, so a 16-bit stream reached a 32-bit I2S endpoint with no
converter in the device graph; that test (v9) reset the phone.

Let playback streams be S32_LE as well, so a stream can be 32 bit end to
end. The AudioReach media-format code already handles a 32-bit width
(bits_per_sample 32, q_factor 31, PCM_LSB_ALIGNED) for the shared-memory
endpoint, PCM decoder/converter and MFC. Capture stays S16/S24.

The front-end DAI from the topology must list S32_LE too (its caps are
ANDed with these): devices/oneplus-waffle/tplg/OnePlus-12-waffle.m4 does
that for MultiMedia2.

Upstream-Status: Pending [needs a test on hardware first]
Tested: not yet (applies to waffle-voice 9359fc74 + 0001-0003)

---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -225,7 +225,8 @@
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_PAUSE | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_RESUME |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_NO_REWINDS | SNDRV_PCM_INFO_SYNC_APPLPTR |
 				 SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH),
-	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE),
+	.formats =              (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |
+				 SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE),
 	.rates =                SNDRV_PCM_RATE_8000_192000,
 	.rate_min =             8000,
 	.rate_max =             192000,
@@ -764,6 +765,11 @@
 	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE:
 		prtd->bits_per_sample = 24;
 		break;
+	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE:
+		if (substream->stream != SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		prtd->bits_per_sample = 32;
+		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
